* A symbol defined with -a= that the source sets too: before the source's first set it has the
* -a= value, and ifdef/ifndef see it defined (an ifndef block that sets it is skipped), as r68
* takes it (measured 2026-10-18; without -a= the final value, as before). Before, the source's
* set made it a symbol not set yet there: the final value, and the ifndef block assembled.
* fixed: 98c270f 2026-10-18 r68togas: an -a= symbol the source sets too has its -a= value before
* options: -a=Rv=2
* expect text: 0002 1111 0005 0006
 psect a_set,0,0,0,0,0
 dc.w Rv
 ifdef Rv
 dc.w $1111
 endc
 ifndef Rv
 dc.w $2222
Rv set 9
 endc
Rv set 5
 dc.w Rv
Rv set Rv+1
 dc.w Rv
 ends
